High above the heavens, a celestial ticker broadcasts price constellations to myriad dashboard deities. The ticker maintains a list of registered listeners and calls them in a loop:

```java
public void publish(Price price) {
    for (PriceListener listener : listeners) {
        listener.onPrice(price);
    }
}
```

Which statements about this design are correct?

Legends speak of a cursed configuration relic hidden within a web citadel, accessed by every request handler. Its ancient code reads:

```java
public class AppConfig {
    private static AppConfig instance;
    private AppConfig() { }
    public static AppConfig getInstance() {
        if (instance == null) {
            instance = new AppConfig();
        }
        return instance;
    }
}
```

Which criticisms of this relic are justified?
